{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "c5dcd8b9-1c68-4315-82b2-0c1496dd1e70"/*FaceLandmarkDetectionExample*/,
  "Description": "Detects faces in a live camera image and shows the built-in debug view: the camera frame with the dense 478-point face mesh of every detected face.\n\nTurn [Debug] off to get the clean camera image on [OutputTexture]. The mesh is provided as data: [PointBuffer] holds 478 points per face in centered image coordinates (Y up, roughly -1..1), each point carrying its mesh index in F1 - see the MediaPipe FaceMesh topology for landmark indices (e.g. 168 = bridge of the nose, 13/14 = inner lips). [FaceCount] holds the number of faces.\n\nFace meshes are small on screen; move close to the camera for a stable dense mesh.",
  "InputUis": [],
  "SymbolChildUis": [
    {
      "ChildId": "1d597e6d-1be9-40fd-a0fd-cc76e09a3de5",
      "SymbolName": "Lib.io.video.WebcamInput",
